    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d476-a5">

                <pb facs="1297" n="1291" xml:id="pg1291"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5 in No. 20½.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Without signature to Mr. Willis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs,<lb/>Honolulu, Hawaiian
                            Islands</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-01-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 1,
                    1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your Excellency’s communication of December
                    29, inquiring if my note amounted to a withdrawal of my communication on the
                    subject referred to, has been received.</p>
                <p>It was not my intention to withdraw any of my letters, but merely to inform you
                    that the arrival of newspaper copies of the special message of the President of
                    the United States on the Hawaiian matter, made it unnecessary for me to press
                    you for further answer to my question.</p>
                <p>With the highest appreciation of your kindly interest, I have the honor,
                    etc.,</p>
                <closer>____________<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#italic">Minister of Foreign
                            Affairs.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>(Not signed.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
